THE LAWS OF DELTANIA
Last revised by the Crown of Anacreon

I.  THE KING'S PEACE
    The killing of another player is lawful only within the Arena of
    Itrius or upon the field of open war.  Murder elsewhere brands the
    killer KILLER, and the City Watch of Itrius is sworn to hunt such
    folk within the city walls.  The theft of a citizen's goods marks
    a THIEF in like manner.

II. THE CROWN'S PROPERTY
    Using bugs to duplicate gold, equipment or experience is theft
    from the Crown.  Report what you find; do not spend it.

III. THE SHARED AIR
    Shouting, griefing, or fouling the public channels is disorderly
    conduct.  The immortal magistrates may silence offenders.

IV.  ONE SOUL, ONE PLAYER
    More than one character played by one person from one house is
    forbidden without the Crown's written leave (email help@deltamud.net).

V.   THE OMNISCIENT CROWN
    Immortals may watch, judge, and reward.  Impersonating one is a
    hanging matter.  Asking for levels, gold, or equipment is beneath
    a hero and will be refused.

VI.  THE Jailer's Door
    Player killing within the jail, cheating the bail system, or
    escaping the Arena forfeits all winnings.

Signed under the seal of the Crown of Anacreon,
in the year the roads were finally safe.
